ection/632731fa65e6b90a208a76fb3820bb6e07668037305d94de586fa49ee3c00b4a" :answer-field/choices ["q-126744/selection/632731fa65e6b90a208a76fb3820bb6e07668037305d94de586fa49ee3c00b4a" "q-126744/selection/83c49809c9efcd775923a709ce756aa8f91caeefb7b6bf23bc9d22bdef5c74da" "q-126744/selection/9d0feacd4dd802e79b8213e734fc54c6cd515c18118f1cf618a327f0ff75b7ea" "q-126744/selection/db4ed159f5ac6e3d303fcd365b2384d85f8efb3ef2f52c1708749efcef608ade" "q-126744/selection/428579e02d9950e0338ab73e5c6585ed702a7ba96a16c03c7ec35db581682fdb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126744" :question/id #uuid "36087a77-de9c-54d4-8570-665799a1fd10" :question/math-academy-id "q-126744" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $F(-5,-2,4)$ and $G(3,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $F$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=f+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $f$ is the position vector of $F.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $F(-5,-2,4)$ and $G(3,-1,1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{FG} \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,1⟩-⟨-5,-2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,1,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126744/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126744"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162161/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "6c3799d7-c7a4-5b2e-befb-8bdb8d9e6b2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162161/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "66342827-5cf6-5474-a1ba-b18b10cf0657" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162161/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "628e0ac7-80df-58b4-b9fa-7967af50269b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162161/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a2ae006f-c6a9-5627-9216-93223ef50594" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162161/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "0a9efbb5-889d-5a01-a06f-edb9b9fe99f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162161/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3dc93760-d0b0-5810-85f8-61f6441f9783" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162161/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-162161/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-162161/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-162161/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-162161/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-162161/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162161" :question/id #uuid "f673252d-f985-582f-b040-6f3a954cdf57" :question/math-academy-id "q-162161" :question/problem "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(3,0,-2)$ and $Q(1,1,-1).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ b \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the  line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=3+1+0=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162161/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f78fe749-e37e-53f2-879f-4c36931c1d6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162161"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
